            "Here is what happened:",
            "→ The new format used fields the hub did not store\n→ Mapping workarounds grew complex and fragile\n→ Change requests queued, and costs began to rise\n→ The BA assessed fit for current and future needs\n→ Leaders weighed a rebuild against a phased upgrade",
            "The stakeholder said:\n\"It worked last year, why can it not work now?\"",
            "So the BA showed how the need had moved, how far the hub could stretch, and what each path would cost in effort and risk, so leaders chose with open eyes.",
            "Why?",
            "Fitness fades when needs move. A solution can be well built for its first purpose and still be the wrong fit for the next purpose. The BA checks fit against present and near future needs, states the stretch limits plainly, and avoids dressing up a major rebuild as a minor tweak.",
            "A solution that fit yesterday may not fit tomorrow.",
            "BA Takeaway",
            "→ Check fit against current and near future needs\n→ Name what the solution cannot stretch to cover\n→ Compare phased upgrade with rebuild honestly\n→ Warn early when a tweak is really a rebuild",
